{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk","id":1525625,"title":"[W5] Fixing Harano and Hauglosk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-19T01:06:52-08:00","id":1525625,"title":"[W5] Fixing Harano and Hauglosk","content":"While I don't mind Harano and Hauglosk as much as some of you, I do think they need to be fixed, just like Touchstones had to be fixed in V5*. I also think that Touchstones in W5 could be better integrated with the H&amp;H mechanics.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* In V5, we introduced a simple house rule for the Touchstone system. Dealing with a Touchstone in a meaningful way (doesn't have to be an interaction, but it should be relevant to play) adds +2 dice to the session's Remorse check. This way, Touchstones serve as a reminder for the PCs what it means to be human. This house rule made Touchstones more meaningful to us and gave a mechanical reason why a character would want to have Touchstones.</span><br /> \u200b<br /> In that sense, I want to overhaul the H&amp;H mechanic in a way to bring it more in line with what I think makes sense without discarding it altogether. So, my basic idea is to make H&amp;H more similar to Humanity with its Remorse checks.<ul><li>Characters still have the five-box Harano and Hauglosk tracker. However, there are temporary versions of both stats... Let's call them &quot;Anguish&quot; for Harano and &quot;Fervor&quot; for Hauglosk. Basically, temporary Anguish and Fervor serve in a similar function as Stains in V5.</li> <li>Points of Anguish and Fervor are marked by a &quot;/&quot; on their respective trackers. If the tracker is filled completely, Anguish is transformed into one box of Harano, Fervor is transformed into one box of Hauglosk.</li> <li>Harano or Hauglosk are permanent, the box is filled completely.</li> </ul><b>Anguish &amp; Harano:</b><ul><li>Characters can gain Anguish, if they experience major setbacks or other tragedies (number of points determined by the ST).</li> <li>The character gains two Anguish if one of their Touchstones is damaged by their action. If one of their Touchstones is killed by their action, the character gains three Anguish.</li> <li>Once per session, the player can opt to voluntarily mark down one Anguish to immediately increase their Rage to 5.</li> <li>Players can make a Harano test for their character (usually at the end of the session). They roll a number dice equal to the <i><b>unfilled </b></i>boxes on their Harano tracker (minimum 1). Having dealt with a Touchstone in a meaningful way before making the check adds 2 dice to this roll. If the test fails, the character gains one point of Harano; if the test is successful, all Anguish is removed from the tracker (permanent Harano remains).</li> <li>If the tracker is completely filled with points of Harano, the character succumbs to harano, leaving the game as a playable character.</li> </ul><b>Fervor &amp; Hauglosk:</b><ul><li>Characters can gain Fervor, if they violate a chronicle tenet (number of points determined by the ST).</li> <li>The character gains two Fervor if one of their Touchstones is damaged by their inaction. If one of their Touchstones is killed by their inaction, the character gains three Fervor.</li> <li>Once per session, the player can opt to voluntarily mark down one Fervor to immediately restore all Willpower damage.</li> <li>Players can make a Hauglosk test for their character (usually at the end of the session). They roll a number dice equal to the <i><b>unfilled </b></i>boxes on their Hauglosk tracker (minimum 1). Having dealt with a Touchstone in a meaningful way before making the check adds 2 dice to this roll. If the test fails, the character gains one point of Hauglosk; if the test is successful, all Fervor is removed from the tracker (permanent Hauglosk remains).</li> <li>If the tracker is completely filled with points of Hauglosk, the character succumbs to hauglosk, leaving the game as a playable character.</li> </ul><br /> What do you think?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 11-19-2023, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T01:31:55-08:00","id":1525628,"title":"","content":"I think if you don't want to make any huge changes,it's not a bad way to extend the doom-spiral long enough that most characters are never going to get removed from the game via the trackers without exceeding bad luck, or specific effort to drive them over the edge.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the &quot;take 1 Anguish/Fervor&quot; for points in other places mechanic is worth keeping. While it's a nice little carrot to temp players to dip their toes in the water instead of avoiding gaining tracker points at all costs, it doesn't really make any sense in a narrative sense of what the character is actually doing. It feels like the mechanic should be reversed to something like, &quot;if you would lose a point of Anguish/Fervor, you can opt instead to max your Rage/Willpower&quot; for something that you can really envision as to what's happening in the PCs' heads. &quot;Instead of completely letting go of my failure, unhealthily cling to some of the guilt as a splinter that drives me to anger,&quot; is something that you wouldn't consciously think of doing but something people definitely do. Likewise holding on to a bit of Fervor as drive more considered and thoughtful actions that still push towards your goals is something that makes sense. But as it stands, you get sad to get angry, and you get angry to emotionally center yourself... which is a very odd mental process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T02:03:48-08:00","id":1525629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525628#post1525628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure the &quot;take 1 Anguish/Fervor&quot; for points in other places mechanic is worth keeping. While it's a nice little carrot to temp players to dip their toes in the water instead of avoiding gaining tracker points at all costs, it doesn't really make any sense in a narrative sense of what the character is actually doing. It feels like the mechanic should be reversed to something like, &quot;if you would lose a point of Anguish/Fervor, you can opt instead to max your Rage/Willpower&quot; for something that you can really envision as to what's happening in the PCs' heads. &quot;Instead of completely letting go of my failure, unhealthily cling to some of the guilt as a splinter that drives me to anger,&quot; is something that you wouldn't consciously think of doing but something people definitely do. Likewise holding on to a bit of Fervor as drive more considered and thoughtful actions that still push towards your goals is something that makes sense. But as it stands, you get sad to get angry, and you get angry to emotionally center yourself... which is a very odd mental process.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. I have to think about it.<br /> <br /> I mean, the way it was written originally (and I adapted it), it's just one of those mechanical bits to play with, taking a disadvantage to get an advantage. But from a narrative perspective, you're completely right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T08:09:39-08:00","id":1525635,"title":"","content":"For myself the biggest improvement to the game is to discard the entire H/H subsystem. But I'm happy to see you've managed to build something that works for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T09:05:51-08:00","id":1525637,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, any &quot;character leaves play&quot; options outside death feel forced to me. As does the permanence of the points. Because shit happens and the longer the chronicles is the more chances to get those filled through no fault of the players there are.<br /> <br /> If this is designed for short chronicles, then sure, it works. But it still implies there is no recovery from trauma (Harano) or extremism (Hauglosk.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T10:17:38-08:00","id":1525640,"title":"","content":"I do wonder what kind of chronicles they were writing this around. A mid sized chronicle is 20-30 sessions for me and I've ran games for hundreds of sessions where the protagonists managed to die, become elders and/or be replaced by a next generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T10:40:31-08:00","id":1525641,"title":"","content":"Josh Heath on a podcast mentioned that the rules for Rage dice he playtested for W5 were more punishing than the version we got in the eventual release. That's an indication of what direction this was aiming for. Harano and Hauglosk are there to punish players. And you can see that in how much of a doomspiral they are you can't come back from.<br /> <br /> As for the mechanics, I'm not a fan. Hauglosk only triggering through Chronicle Tenets should require a more directed discussion of those in the storytelling chapter rather than the general one we got. Harano is linked to Touchstones in a way I don't like as it mechanically urges STs to threaten/harm/kill Touchstones. It feels cheap to forcefully push for that in order to link between players and the Harano mechanic.<br /> <br /> I thought about coming up with my own version but there's just so much that needs to be tweaked and expanded even while staying in the realm of how V5 was designed... It just didn't feel worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T10:41:30-08:00","id":1525642,"title":"","content":"We don't need to wonder; the target and purpose was almost undoubtedly &quot;make it like Vampire&quot;, possibly with the amendment of &quot;...but worse.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:12:15-08:00","id":1525645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525642#post1525642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't need to wonder; the target and purpose was almost undoubtedly &quot;make it like Vampire&quot;, possibly with the amendment of &quot;...but worse.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, both H5 and W5 have a weird take on V5 systems. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"387\" data-vbnamecard=\"387\">Caldorian</a>already mentioned some of these. Humanity, Stains, Convictions, Ambitions etc. It's just weird how often the design decisions tended to do less than V5. Not take V5 and try to expand or adapt systems but try to do less. Always gave me the impression that with both H5 and W5 the developers didn't have much faith in the system they were using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:17:07-08:00","id":1525646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525637#post1525637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty, any &quot;character leaves play&quot; options outside death feel forced to me. As does the permanence of the points. Because shit happens and the longer the chronicles is the more chances to get those filled through no fault of the players there are.<br /> <br /> If this is designed for short chronicles, then sure, it works. But it still implies there is no recovery from trauma (Harano) or extremism (Hauglosk.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There have always been these types of trackers. Sanity in Call of Cthulhu, Dark Side in the old WEG Star Wars game. While I understand a fundamental dislike for such mechanics, nothing is keeping the ST from allowing the other PCs to redeem or heal a &quot;fallen&quot; characters through an appropriate quest.<br /> <br /> For me, &quot;leaving play&quot; just means that the characters is not playable for a while.<br /> <br /> YMMV, of course, but it's not like the story police will knock on your door if you do a redemption arc in your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:28:13-08:00","id":1525648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525641#post1525641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harano is linked to Touchstones in a way I don't like as it mechanically urges STs to threaten/harm/kill Touchstones. It feels cheap to forcefully push for that in order to link between players and the Harano mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, this assumes an antagonistic relationship between ST and players, which almost never happened in the WoD games I played in the past 30 years.<br /> <br /> You could also argue the other way around. It incentivizes players to take better care of their characters' Touchstones, to pay attention to them, protect them, etc. Something that has always been a part of classical WtA games, at least for us (protection of Kinfolk, etc.).<br /> <br /> As a ST, I would only threaten Touchstones, if it made sense in the framework of the story and the PCs were careless about their protection. In general, I think targeting Touchstones just to cause Stains/Anguish/Fervor would be a shitty move for ST. I mean, it's not like I have an interest, as a ST, to drive PCs towards harano and hauglosk. H&amp;H should serve more as swords of Damocles hanging over PCs, building tension and narrative drive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:37:49-08:00","id":1525649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525648#post1525648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, this assumes an antagonistic relationship between ST and players, which almost never happened in the WoD games I played in the past 30 years.<br /> <br /> You could also argue the other way around. It incentivizes players to take better care of their characters' Touchstones, to pay attention to them, protect them, etc. Something that has always been a part of classical WtA games, at least for us (protection of Kinfolk, etc.).<br /> <br /> As a ST, I would only threaten Touchstones, if it made sense in the framework of the story and the PCs were careless about their protection. In general, I think targeting Touchstones just to cause Stains/Anguish/Fervor would be a shitty move for ST. I mean, it's not like I have an interest, as a ST, to drive PCs towards harano and hauglosk. H&amp;H should serve more as swords of Damocles hanging over PCs, building tension and narrative drive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Kinfolk have been removed and Touchstones as ties to humanity is a VtM thing, not a WtA thing. Additionally, the Touchstones mechanics with their once per story mechanic don't work as intended. There's no benefit to multiple Touchstones while it creates more opportunities for Harano tests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:53:10-08:00","id":1525653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525649#post1525649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that Kinfolk have been removed and Touchstones as ties to humanity is a VtM thing, not a WtA thing. Additionally, the Touchstones mechanics with their once per story mechanic don't work as intended. There's no benefit to multiple Touchstones while it creates more opportunities for Harano tests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's because I'm currently reading the TJ Klune's Green Creek series, where werewolves have &quot;tethers&quot; that prevent them from going feral, but I actually like the introduction of Touchstones for WtA. I like having a cast of secondary characters, an &quot;extended pack&quot; with which the PCs regularly interact.<br /> <br /> I mean, in previous versions kinfolk were always part of the equation. Sure, there are no kinfolk anymore (although that's something left open to interpretation, since there seem to be lineages who produce more Garou), but I like it if a game keeps characters more grounded by binding them stronger to the larger world. We always played like that, whether in WtA or Exalted.<br /> <br /> The benefit of multiple Touchstones with this house rule is that you still have a Touchstone if something should happen to another. Or, even more simply, you have more options when trying to get the +2 bonus for H&amp;H tests. (For instance, when one Touchstone is not available for whatever reason.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T12:35:50-08:00","id":1525654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525653#post1525653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's because I'm currently reading the TJ Klune's Green Creek series, where werewolves have &quot;tethers&quot; that prevent them from going feral, but I actually like the introduction of Touchstones for WtA. I like having a cast of secondary characters, an &quot;extended pack&quot; with which the PCs regularly interact.<br /> <br /> I mean, in previous versions kinfolk were always part of the equation. Sure, there are no kinfolk anymore (although that's something left open to interpretation, since there seem to be lineages who produce more Garou), but I like it if a game keeps characters more grounded by binding them stronger to the larger world. We always played like that, whether in WtA or Exalted.<br /> <br /> The benefit of multiple Touchstones with this house rule is that you still have a Touchstone if something should happen to another. Or, even more simply, you have more options when trying to get the +2 bonus for H&amp;H tests. (For instance, when one Touchstone is not available for whatever reason.)</div> </div> </div> </div>WtF 2E actually did that with Wolf-Blooded as &quot;more useful version of Kinfolk who are also part of the Pack&quot;. I like the idea of a WtA-Touchstones-equivalent being more about non-Werewolf-allies who volunteer to help the Garou's cause rather than Garou needing Touchstones to tie themselves to humanity. WtF has a good update on the Kinfolk-concept in that respect, I think. I wish they had carried over the idea from WtF to W5 that a Pack isn't just the Garou and maybe their Patron-Spirit. But then again the developers somehow looked at Coterie-types in V5 and didn't immediately make the connection to introducing Pack-types in W5 (another example of just leaving a desgin-concept from V5 on the table)...<br /> <br /> With vampires, the Beast, the Masquerade and Humanity maintaining Touchstones has a different goal which also translates to what sort of Touchstones you have. With Garou I like the idea more of what's &quot;grounding&quot; about their version of Touchstones is that they remind Garou that they aren't alone in their fight to save Gaia. And that's what's preventing them from giving in to Harano. It isn't about Garou needing a reminder of what it's like to be human. The reason is that what I think needs to be emphasized is how Garou are warriors who are fighting a holy war. In WtF you have &quot;the wolf must hunt&quot;, with WtA you have the war against the Wyrm (with the emphasis on war).<br /> <br /> As for Kinfolk in W5... the way it's set up is now you have Kin and Garou. Kin are would-be werewolves and (for whatever reason) it's still indicated that in a lot of cases, someone is a Kin because they are related to Garou. And then sometimes it's just some random person who becomes a Kin for whatever reason. But there isn't this community WtA had before. Although, it's also dubious how Silver Fangs exactly work in this new paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T16:31:13-08:00","id":1525666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525646#post1525646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There have always been these types of trackers. Sanity in Call of Cthulhu, Dark Side in the old WEG Star Wars game. While I understand a fundamental dislike for such mechanics, nothing is keeping the ST from allowing the other PCs to redeem or heal a &quot;fallen&quot; characters through an appropriate quest.<br /> <br /> For me, &quot;leaving play&quot; just means that the characters is not playable for a while.<br /> <br /> YMMV, of course, but it's not like the story police will knock on your door if you do a redemption arc in your chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't state that there is a possibility for the PC to return to play, though. Just that they leave play. As weird as it is to say this, the addition of &quot;the pack can do a redemption quest to return the character to play&quot; can help a lot to control the tone of the game.<br /> <br /> While this is not your fault, tying Hauglosk to Chronicle Tenets is a bad idea. Chronicle Tenets can be the mood of the chronicle OR they can be a &quot;Hey, I don't want to see this in the game, please&quot; reminders. While naturally a smart player will not use THOSE tenets to gain Hauglosk, the lack of thought of that in the text is still a problem.<br /> <br /> As much as I like the idea of having human tethers to tie the garou into humanity, there is still a playable tribe that's focused on destroying humanity and now even openly eats humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T23:45:07-08:00","id":1525674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525666#post1525666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You didn't state that there is a possibility for the PC to return to play, though. Just that they leave play. As weird as it is to say this, the addition of &quot;the pack can do a redemption quest to return the character to play&quot; can help a lot to control the tone of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point. I will include it when I formalize the house rules for my group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525666#post1525666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this is not your fault, tying Hauglosk to Chronicle Tenets is a bad idea. Chronicle Tenets can be the mood of the chronicle OR they can be a &quot;Hey, I don't want to see this in the game, please&quot; reminders. While naturally a smart player will not use THOSE tenets to gain Hauglosk, the lack of thought of that in the text is still a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, well Chronicle Tenets aren't those things though. Not completely anyway. One big part is that they're the chronicle's morality gauge. In that sense, they can set the mood of the chronicle as well.* At least, that's what they are in V5, and how I understand them here as well. In that sense, the connection between hauglosk and the Tenets does make sense (to me, at least). If you abandon the chronicle's ethical framework, you drift into the manic extremism of hauglosk.<br /> <br /> * In my current V5 chronicle, a 1920s Prohibition era horror/gangster story, the tenets really inform PC behavior in my experience. The whole Tenet concept is much better integrated in V5, because you can avoid Stains when killing, depending on the Tenets, but I think it could work here as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525666#post1525666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like the idea of having human tethers to tie the garou into humanity, there is still a playable tribe that's focused on destroying humanity and now even openly eats humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, wolves can be Touchstones as well. So, Touchstones are not about humanity, they are about tethering the Garou to something material.<br /> <br /> Based on me liking the Green Creek series, I'm actually also thinking about house ruling the system to allow other Garou (packmates, mentors) who are not in harano or hauglosk to act as Touchstones as well. I feel emphasizing the &quot;found family&quot; aspect of packs and how the community grounds you could improve the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 11-20-2023, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T00:56:49-08:00","id":1525677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525674#post1525674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, well Chronicle Tenets aren't those things though. Not completely anyway. One big part is that they're the chronicle's morality gauge. In that sense, they can set the mood of the chronicle as well.* At least, that's what they are in V5, and how I understand them here as well. In that sense, the connection between hauglosk and the Tenets does make sense (to me, at least). If you abandon the chronicle's ethical framework, you drift into the manic extremism of hauglosk.<br /> <br /> * In my current V5 chronicle, a 1920s Prohibition era horror/gangster story, the tenets really inform PC behavior in my experience. The whole Tenet concept is much better integrated in V5, because you can avoid Stains when killing, depending on the Tenets, but I think it could work here as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morality gauge can also mean the amount of darkness the players are okay with.<br /> <br /> I know what I'm saying sounds rather odd, but rules should take into account situations where they can conflict with the intention of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525674#post1525674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, wolves can be Touchstones as well. So, Touchstones are not about humanity, they are about tethering the Garou to something material.<br /> <br /> Based on me liking the Green Creek series, I'm actually also thinking about house ruling the system to allow other Garou (packmates, mentors) who are not in harano or hauglosk to act as Touchstones as well. I feel emphasizing the &quot;found family&quot; aspect of packs and how the community grounds you could improve the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a GREAT idea. It would also support the sense of a pack relying on each other for sanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T04:01:39-08:00","id":1525718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525674#post1525674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, well Chronicle Tenets aren't those things though. Not completely anyway. One big part is that they're the chronicle's morality gauge. In that sense, they can set the mood of the chronicle as well.* At least, that's what they are in V5, and how I understand them here as well. In that sense, the connection between hauglosk and the Tenets does make sense (to me, at least). If you abandon the chronicle's ethical framework, you drift into the manic extremism of hauglosk.<br /> <br /> * In my current V5 chronicle, a 1920s Prohibition era horror/gangster story, the tenets really inform PC behavior in my experience. The whole Tenet concept is much better integrated in V5, because you can avoid Stains when killing, depending on the Tenets, but I think it could work here as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think personally I wouldn't go with the way it's presented in the V5 corebook and the W5 corebook but the way it's presented in the V5 Players Guide. From pg 205:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although they seem similar to Chronicle Tenets, the character\u2019s Convictions have a different purpose narratively, mechanically, and philosophically. The Tenets deny (\u201cThou shalt not kill\u201d) while Convictions permit (\u201cProtect the marginalized\u201d), creating drama from the conflict. This shows up explicitly the mechanics: If you violate a Tenet in service of your Conviction, it reduces the resulting Stains by one or more (Vampire: The Masquerade, p. 239). They define where your own beliefs may stray or more strongly converge from those of society or even your comrades.<br /> <br /> Convictions are often statements that start with the word \u201calways\u201d or \u201cnever\u201d, they deal in absolutes because they illustrate core pillars of a character\u2019s identity and what anchors them to their remaining Humanity. Storytellers should deny Convictions that are overly vague or open-ended. At base, Convictions should be short, powerful reasons to justify Tenet transgressions.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I think the described dynamic from that section is what should also be reproduced for what is furthering Hauglosk in W5. And I think that's why I would bring back Convictions to make this work: The tenets are restrictive and forbidding and yet there are reasons to cross those lines with personal motivations explaining why you still would wanna cross those lines. It certainly puts Tenets as indicators of the mood of the game on the backburner but the aforementioned way works better with Tenets being part of a mechanic, I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T05:25:12-08:00","id":1525721,"title":"","content":"Good points!<br /> <br /> Just to let you know, I haven't abandoned this topic, I'm just still mulling over the very good points you made, but haven't come up with good ideas how to tackle the issues yet.<br /> <br /> Reintroducing Convictions seems like a good idea. I've also thought about how to reinstall pack patrons, so maybe these could be combined with Convictions as well? (With Tribe bans being more like Tenets.) Just a spontaneous idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T00:38:03-08:00","id":1525775,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I have found some solutions for me, but I don't think this community is conducive for discussing W5. Thanks anyway for all the input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 11-22-2023, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T06:02:18-08:00","id":1525788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1525721#post1525721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points!<br /> <br /> Just to let you know, I haven't abandoned this topic, I'm just still mulling over the very good points you made, but haven't come up with good ideas how to tackle the issues yet.<br /> <br /> Reintroducing Convictions seems like a good idea. I've also thought about how to reinstall pack patrons, so maybe these could be combined with Convictions as well? (With Tribe bans being more like Tenets.) Just a spontaneous idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another idea for dealing with these I also had was to bring back ambition and desire. With the short term goal being another way to heal WP and the long term goal allowing a PC to erase a point of Harano or hauglosk. Additionally, you can also do that when you present the success of a mission at a Moot or otherwise any gathering with a receptive audience. The idea is to push the theme of &quot;getting shit done &quot; as an antidote to Harano and Hauglosk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T15:05:33-08:00","id":1526300,"title":"","content":"I have finished compiling the first version of my house rules: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/1mprhi0zl3yc4bwstz29q/House-Rules-v1.1.pdf?rlkey=5995y1t2vuywkxmosdapxota7&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Dropbox link to PDF</a><br /> <br /> My goal is to bring W5 back a bit more to the legacy setting while making better use of various bits and pieces of 5e mechanics.<br /> <br /> I included the Anguish and Fervor rules, but they are flanked by other changes.<br /> <br /> I'd appreciate some constructive feedback. \ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-04-2023, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T05:01:07-08:00","id":1526352,"title":"","content":"While walking my dog this morning, it occurred to me that I should add a third compulsion... the Hunt.<br /> <br /> If you have any other good ideas, please let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T05:37:27-08:00","id":1526354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526352#post1526352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While walking my dog this morning, it occurred to me that I should add a third compulsion... the Hunt.<br /> <br /> If you have any other good ideas, please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not use The Hunt in WtA. WtF has made the Hunt into its core gameplay and W5 already takes so much from it.<br /> <br /> Maybe something like Drive? Since garou are defined by their task by Gaia, drive to do so would make the most sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T12:15:03-08:00","id":1526367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526354#post1526354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would not use The Hunt in WtA. WtF has made the Hunt into its core gameplay and W5 already takes so much from it.<br /> <br /> Maybe something like Drive? Since garou are defined by their task by Gaia, drive to do so would make the most sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not too familiar with WtF. What is the Hunt there?<br /> <br /> Well, the compulsion should represent a primal urge. In this case, the compulsion would require the Garou to hunt something (usually for a scene) or suffer a 2 dice penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T12:20:14-08:00","id":1526368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526367#post1526367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not too familiar with WtF. What is the Hunt there?<br /> <br /> Well, the compulsion should represent a primal urge. In this case, the compulsion would require the Garou to hunt something (usually for a scene) or suffer a 2 dice penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what you described below, the compulsion to hunt something to the point it is a massive cultural touchstone for the werewolves in WtF. The powerstat of the WtF werewolves is in fact called Primal-Urge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T02:40:12-08:00","id":1526394,"title":"","content":"A couple of ideas and comments:<ul><li>For the third Compulsion, I have two ideas: One is a compelled behavior/action related to the PC's Auspice. Haven't really thought about it beyond that but it just came to mind because one of the priorities in houseruling W5 for me would definitely be to make Auspice more relevant. The other idea would be to make it about &quot;The Curse&quot;. Your character just radiates &quot;Hey, I'm a supernatural predator.&quot;. In weak-willed individuals it outright causes Delirium, others just shy away from the character and potential enemies immediately take notice of the character.</li> <li>Linking the Brutal Outcomes to the verbs is all well and good but I think that demands another look at the verbs-list. Some of those aren't very good (Ahroun is particularly egregious, for example). Also, having eight verbs that don't trigger failures in Brutal Outcomes might be too many... Although I'm not sure. This is one of those things you would just have to playtest it and see how it goes.</li> <li>With Chronicle Tenets one thing I've been thinking about is to be way more specific in what you pick. My reason for that is on a principal level the &quot;Tenets deny&quot; should stay but beyond that, for example, picking &quot;Thou shalt not kill&quot; in a V5 game isn't just about picking a principle that denies but also should highlight what people consider to be important about staying true to Humanity.</li> <li>With that in mind, this is how I would re-interpret both Hauglosk and what the Chronicle Tenets represent: The Tenets you pick are picked individually rather than as a group. You go to each player and for the three Tenets ask these three questions: What should a Garou never do? What should a member of your Tribe never do? What should a member of your Auspice never do? (The first one could be picked by the whole group together and you could give multiple answers to each if so desired)</li> <li>And in my headcanon I would redefine Hauglosk to be less about being super-zealous, acting like eco-fascists but instead another way of giving up. Where Harano is a Garou giving up and stopping to fight, Hauglosk is giving up but continuing to fight without any greater cause or higher goal motivating you. Fighting for dominance, survival, some personal selfish goal and also not caring what one does in pursuit of that. And for a lot of Garou this state also ends up as a precursor to joining the BSD.</li> <li>And the Fenrir in that context are more about nihilists who are convinced that Gaia is dead, the Apocalypse is inevitable and so what's the point of stuff like managing a caern, paying obeisance to Patron-Spirits or honoring Gaia? They fight Wyrm-minions because they hold them responsible for the state of the world but they don't think they will defeat the Wyrm or they're pursuing some higher duty or war (and what would even be the point of that at this point?). Roaming around and looking for good fights is all that matters. And what is considered &quot;good&quot; by a Fenrir-Pack in that context could be all sorts of things and varies between Fenrir-Packs.</li> <li>So Hauglosk in this form is more about a werewolf letting go of all that Garou-stuff and just fighting for whatever they care about. You can stop caring about Gaia, the Garou-Nation, caerns, the war against the Wyrm and all that. And bringing someone back from Hauglosk is about making them realize that being a Garou is still a worthy cause and that the traditions of Garou still matter. (Of course, this kinda goes everything W5 is about)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T11:09:36-08:00","id":1526413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526394#post1526394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of ideas and comments:<ul><li>For the third Compulsion, I have two ideas: One is a compelled behavior/action related to the PC's Auspice. Haven't really thought about it beyond that but it just came to mind because one of the priorities in houseruling W5 for me would definitely be to make Auspice more relevant. The other idea would be to make it about &quot;The Curse&quot;. Your character just radiates &quot;Hey, I'm a supernatural predator.&quot;. In weak-willed individuals it outright causes Delirium, others just shy away from the character and potential enemies immediately take notice of the character.</li> <li>Linking the Brutal Outcomes to the verbs is all well and good but I think that demands another look at the verbs-list. Some of those aren't very good (Ahroun is particularly egregious, for example). Also, having eight verbs that don't trigger failures in Brutal Outcomes might be too many... Although I'm not sure. This is one of those things you would just have to playtest it and see how it goes.</li> <li>With Chronicle Tenets one thing I've been thinking about is to be way more specific in what you pick. My reason for that is on a principal level the &quot;Tenets deny&quot; should stay but beyond that, for example, picking &quot;Thou shalt not kill&quot; in a V5 game isn't just about picking a principle that denies but also should highlight what people consider to be important about staying true to Humanity.</li> <li>With that in mind, this is how I would re-interpret both Hauglosk and what the Chronicle Tenets represent: The Tenets you pick are picked individually rather than as a group. You go to each player and for the three Tenets ask these three questions: What should a Garou never do? What should a member of your Tribe never do? What should a member of your Auspice never do? (The first one could be picked by the whole group together and you could give multiple answers to each if so desired)</li> <li>And in my headcanon I would redefine Hauglosk to be less about being super-zealous, acting like eco-fascists but instead another way of giving up. Where Harano is a Garou giving up and stopping to fight, Hauglosk is giving up but continuing to fight without any greater cause or higher goal motivating you. Fighting for dominance, survival, some personal selfish goal and also not caring what one does in pursuit of that. And for a lot of Garou this state also ends up as a precursor to joining the BSD.</li> <li>And the Fenrir in that context are more about nihilists who are convinced that Gaia is dead, the Apocalypse is inevitable and so what's the point of stuff like managing a caern, paying obeisance to Patron-Spirits or honoring Gaia? They fight Wyrm-minions because they hold them responsible for the state of the world but they don't think they will defeat the Wyrm or they're pursuing some higher duty or war (and what would even be the point of that at this point?). Roaming around and looking for good fights is all that matters. And what is considered &quot;good&quot; by a Fenrir-Pack in that context could be all sorts of things and varies between Fenrir-Packs.</li> <li>So Hauglosk in this form is more about a werewolf letting go of all that Garou-stuff and just fighting for whatever they care about. You can stop caring about Gaia, the Garou-Nation, caerns, the war against the Wyrm and all that. And bringing someone back from Hauglosk is about making them realize that being a Garou is still a worthy cause and that the traditions of Garou still matter. (Of course, this kinda goes everything W5 is about)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the comments!<br /> <br /> I like both ideas for the compulsion, but I think I could fold the supernatural predator into the dominance compulsion to differentiate it a bit more from the V5 one (from which I stole it). And while I see the point about the Hunt being a big thing in WtF, I feel it could be combined with the harm compulsion to make it different as well... so, maybe less about hunting something and more about &quot;going for the kill of the perceived weakest link.&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea of bringing in the auspices with the compulsion is interesting, but I think it's thematically not fitting for me yet. I see auspices and tribes as structuring elements that shape a werewolf's Rage into something functional. Compulsions, however, are about getting lost in the darker impulses of Rage for a moment, not completely, but enough to be noticeable. So, it would need to be something related to the darker aspects of the auspices to work for me. So, perhaps harmful mischief for Ragabash, paranoid secrecy for Theurges, paralyzing indecision for Philodox, dishing out harsh criticism for Galliards, and senseless violence for Ahroun... or something like that.<br /> <br /> With regard to the Chronicle Tenets, I think your ideas are interesting and I agree that they should be chosen by the group together but, as a ST, I find it a bit difficult to track all the PCs' Convictions plus a single set of Tenets in my V5 campaign, especially if I have to juggle the plot, so I'm reluctant to complicate it further.<br /> <br /> I really like your redefinition of Hauglosk. If you're okay with it, I would like to add it to my house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T13:16:22-08:00","id":1526416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526413#post1526413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like both ideas for the compulsion, but I think I could fold the supernatural predator into the dominance compulsion to differentiate it a bit more from the V5 one (from which I stole it). And while I see the point about the Hunt being a big thing in WtF, I feel it could be combined with the harm compulsion to make it different as well... so, maybe less about hunting something and more about &quot;going for the kill of the perceived weakest link.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of other ideas:<ul><li>Compelled shifting to the Lupus-Form for a Homid and acting animal-like for a scene. - This is about tying a compulsion to man-wolf-dynamic and Rage overpowering a human-born Garou for a bit and urging them to indulge in their wolf-side. (Inspired by the Gangrel Compulsion)</li> <li>Challenge/Act against someone in the scene who acts against their own Conviction or upsets the spiritual balance of a place (their actions might lead to the creation of Wyrm-Spirits, for example). - It really is a variation of Dominance but more specific and focused on righteousness and spirituality/animism. It's like a more Garou-flavored version but Dominance should stay as a more general option (Inspired by the Assamites Compulsion from the PG)</li> <li>Motivating/Forcing someone else to engage in violence/brutality that furthers the Garou's cause regardless of the consequences. - Not engaging in the Rage-filled behavior counts as well when you can convince or force someone else to do it. It doesn't matter who does it, all that matters is that the commitment to destruction is shown. I like that as an option because then Rage-filled behavior is now not necessarily about your character committing brutal/violent acts. Not every PC needs to be prepared to be the absolute warrior and there's a &quot;social-abilities-focused&quot; version of being compelled by Rage.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526413#post1526413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of bringing in the auspices with the compulsion is interesting, but I think it's thematically not fitting for me yet. I see auspices and tribes as structuring elements that shape a werewolf's Rage into something functional. Compulsions, however, are about getting lost in the darker impulses of Rage for a moment, not completely, but enough to be noticeable. So, it would need to be something related to the darker aspects of the auspices to work for me. So, perhaps harmful mischief for Ragabash, paranoid secrecy for Theurges, paralyzing indecision for Philodox, dishing out harsh criticism for Galliards, and senseless violence for Ahroun... or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my thought is that you would have to rewrite the lore and come up with something like a &quot;moon-curse&quot; or something, that it's part of Luna's blessing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526413#post1526413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regard to the Chronicle Tenets, I think your ideas are interesting and I agree that they should be chosen by the group together but, as a ST, I find it a bit difficult to track all the PCs' Convictions plus a single set of Tenets in my V5 campaign, especially if I have to juggle the plot, so I'm reluctant to complicate it further.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But here's the thing: You're already doing that anyway. And what I mean by that is the Tribe-Bans. Take the Ghost Council Ban:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Horned Serpent is known for Wisdom, but spirits and Garou alike look askance at the ways she garners knowledge. For a scene in which the Ghost Council werewolf <b>has an opportunity</b> to satisfy their curiosity but doesn\u2019t, they regain only a single point of Willpower at the beginning of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.\u200b </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> This Ban already expects an ST to be mindful of &quot;has an opportunity&quot; in regards to a Ghost Council PC. And there are other Bans, of course, which require similar attention. It also doesn't help that even with the two missing Tribes you still have 11 Tribes which is quite a lot of character-options to take into account for what players could potentially choose. And that's also why it made sense for accessibility's sake to move to that 5x5-matrix for character-options in CofD. But oWOD relies on people being invested in lore/worldbuilding and therefore being fine with this huge amount of options. Of course, it's a bit ironic that WOD5E cuts back on lore to such a degree and in the end, you still have the hard math of expecting people to deal with 11 playable Tribes.<br /> <br /> If anything, I would argue the Tribe-Ban should be ditched and instead have it only come up in the form of this Chronicle Tenet. Since this edition was so insistent on ditching the lore, there's room now to just let the player tell you what they want the Tribe to be about specifically. I as ST would prefer that compared to the Tribe-Bans in the book.<br /> <br /> I never liked the idea of linking the WP-thing to Tribe-Bans, to begin with, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526413#post1526413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI really like your redefinition of Hauglosk. If you're okay with it, I would like to add it to my house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, fine with that. That new definition also makes it easier for Harano and Hauglosk to exist in parallel as there's more thematic unity with the new definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T03:32:37-08:00","id":1526512,"title":"","content":"I'm still working in some of the ideas you had. I also thought about revising and possibly shortening the verb list. Do you want to help with that?<br /> <br /> Here's the official list for ease of reference: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTableGrid\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Auspice</span></span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Verbs</span></span></b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Ragabash</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Trick, Misdirect, Mock, Sneak</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Theurge</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Summon, Invoke, Placate, Bind</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Philodox</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Evaluate, Interpret, Punish, Judge</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Galliard</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Regale, Hype, Unite, Bluster</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Ahroun</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Fight, Attack, Destroy, Charge</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Tribe</span></span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Verbs</span></span></b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Black Furies</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Avenge, Overcome, Dismantle, Demolish</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Bone Gnawers</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Infiltrate, Pilfer, Eavesdrop, Witness</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Children of Gaia</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Discover, Discern, Heal, Puzzle Out</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Hart Wardens</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Reclaim, Cultivate, Nurture, Protect</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Galestalkers</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Track, Ambush, Pursue, Harry</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Ghost Council</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Seek, Solve, Subvert, Unearth</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Glass Walkers</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Research, Build, Hack, Repurpose</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Red Talons</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Ruin, Ward, Reduce, Purge</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Shadow Lords</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Envision, Plan, Scheme, Intimidate</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Silent Striders</span></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"color:black\">Journey, Scout, Deliver, Sabotage</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Silver Fangs</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Motivate, Lead, Rally, Inspire</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T14:50:51-08:00","id":1526528,"title":"","content":"If your going to adjust that, have you considered changing from verb + verb to something like verb + noun or verb + adverb?<br /> <br /> Which changes from verbs isn't really that important, but in the end you get a much more evocative sense of what a Auspice + Tribe pairing is by mixing parts of speech than just having a long list of verbs (even if you cut them down to three each, it's still six verbs that can get pretty repetitive with certain picks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T23:02:42-08:00","id":1526547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526528#post1526528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your going to adjust that, have you considered changing from verb + verb to something like verb + noun or verb + adverb?<br /> <br /> Which changes from verbs isn't really that important, but in the end you get a much more evocative sense of what a Auspice + Tribe pairing is by mixing parts of speech than just having a long list of verbs (even if you cut them down to three each, it's still six verbs that can get pretty repetitive with certain picks).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty open in that regard. It was actually one of my first impulses when thinking about cleaning up the list.<br /> <br /> A lot of the verbs seem redundant because they try to cover a range of activities that would be covered by a noun (basically a role). So, you have all these similar verbs for Ahroun that basically boil down to &quot;warrior&quot; or &quot;fighter.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think in the promo material they talked about Tribe being <i>what</i> you do and Auspice <i>how</i> you do it, right? So, in that sense it's probably easy to chunk these verbs together in a way to make it more concise and even more open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T00:38:31-08:00","id":1526548,"title":"","content":"Verbs + Adverbs also give you more &quot;actions&quot; to build ideas off of. Three Ahroun adverbs with three Tribal verbs gets you nine total ideas instead of six. Nouns are probably easier, but adverbs does get into the &quot;how&quot; vs. &quot;what&quot; dynamic you pointed to. if Silver Fangs &quot;lead&quot; how does each Auspice express leading? If Ahrouns doing things &quot;bluntly&quot; you can get some interesting contrasts between the more aggressive Tribes like the Black Furies and Red Talons, vs. ones like the Children of Gaia (how does your Ahroun &quot;heal blunty?&quot; as a concept).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T10:56:51-08:00","id":1526560,"title":"","content":"I did a breakdown of the Tribe-verbs when the preview came out over a year ago:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glory</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Honor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wisdom</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Stealth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Shadow Lords</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Bone Gnawers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glass Walkers</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fight/Confront</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Black Furies</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Galestalkers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ghost Council</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Community</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">(Get of Fenris)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Silver Fangs</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Silent Striders</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Protect</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fianna</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Red Talons</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Children Of Gaia</td> </tr> </table></div> Now the logic here is that there are two traits: The Renown and a specific way to express the Renown. The way I got the four categories on the left is:<ul><li>Stealth are Tribes that have verbs about doing things secretly or using subterfuge (SL: scheme, BG: Eavesdrop, GW: Hack)</li> <li>Fight/Confront are Tribes that look to engage enemies (BF: Overcome/Demolish, Gale: Ambush, GhoC: Subvert)</li> <li>Community are Tribes that do something that benefits other Garou (SF: Inspire, SiSt: Deliver (ie being messengers))</li> <li>Protect are Tribes that have verbs for defending (Fi: Protect, RT: Ward, CoG: Heal)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Now as for Renowns, I think there are also similarities:<ul><li>Glory Tribes have aspirational verbs about achieving some future goal (SL: Envision, BF: Avenge, Fi: Reclaim)</li> <li>Honor Tribes are about contributing a service to Garou society (BG: Witness, GS: Track (ie tracking down enemies), SF: Motivate, RT: Purge)</li> <li>Wisdom Tribes deal with the occult secrets of the world (including the Umbra) (GW: Research, GhoC: Unearth, SiSt: Scout, CoG: Puzzle Out)</li> </ul>__________________________________________<br /> <br /> This could be a starting-point. A 4x3-grid with one verb expressing the Tribe's focus on a particular Renown-type and another verb expressing a particular category as outlined by the matrix. That way the Tribe-verbs would already be reduced from four to two. Of course, when I wrote that last year it was more meant as an analysis of the verbs listed in the preview than an actual model for how to deal with the Tribes. It's a beginning but there's still a lot to think about...<br /> <br /> As for the Auspices, I agree with HeavyArms that limiting this to just verbs doesn't make much sense. Honestly never understood the insistence on this having to be verbs. So I have two ideas:<ul><li>Specific phrases describing activities associated with each Auspice. There's even precedence for that: The Coterie-Types in the V5 Players Guide were described with short phrases as well.</li> <li>The other idea I have is that you go to Renown-related stuff but link it to blatantly stealing something from Forsaken: Five types of Renown. So it would go: Ragabash - Cunning, Theurge - Wisdom, Philodox - Honor, Galliard - Glory, Ahroun - Purity. And not to confuse things with the three Renowns in the game, here are some alternative names: Trickster, Sage, Mediator, Vanguard, Ideal. Not sure about the last two. Maybe someone has better ideas for those names. But the narrative reasoning is that acting like that is a Garou perfectly impersonating their Auspice and that's how you justify the Brutal-Outcome-bit.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T12:24:17-08:00","id":1526622,"title":"","content":"Okay, I was traveling and playing our V5 campaign this weekend, so I'm behind on integrating all your feedback.<br /> <br /> Here's the subchapter &quot;Hauglosk Redefined&quot;. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;In the rulebook hauglosk is defined as a \u201cstate of extreme righteousness\u201d (p. 52), when a werewolf loses \u201call compassion and mercy to the fanaticism of their cause\u201d (p. 140). It is interpreted as a long-term, if not permanent, state of violent extremism that all Garou can fall into. In these house rules, the state of hauglosk is redefined.<br /> <br /> Instead of a spiritual state of fanaticism, hauglosk is understood as another way of resignation, of giving up on the cause of fighting for Gaia. Harano and hauglosk now represent two dysfunctional strategies of dealing with the hopelessness Garou feel when confronted with the Apocalypse. Whereas harano is all about internalizing their rage and despair, hauglosk is all about externalizing them by acting out.<br /> <br /> In essence, harano is a spiritual state of depression and learned helplessness, when utter despair makes Garou give up on themselves and Gaia, stopping to fight altogether, withdrawing into themselves, and accepting their doom. In contrast, hauglosk is a spiritual state of nihilism and moral disengagement, when complete disillusionment and overwhelming rage make Garou abandon their fight for a greater cause or higher goal. After all, if Gaia is dead and the Apocalypse is inevitable, what\u2019s the point of honoring the spirits, protecting and nurturing caerns, or upholding Garou traditions? Instead those in hauglosk unleash all their anger and hate on those who have hurt them, on those who they deem inferior, or those who just can easily be hurt. Some Garou in hauglosk recklessly follow their own selfish desires for power, dominance, and survival, without consideration for any collateral damage they might cause. Some just continue to fight and destroy, constantly roaming around and looking for glorious fights, not because they think it makes any difference but because it\u2019s all they\u2019ve ever known. Garou in hauglosk are convinced that they are doomed no matter what they do, so they lash out any way they can. For some Garou, falling into hauglosk ends up as the first step towards joining the Black Spiral Dancers.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Given the redefinition, I now need a more fitting term for Fervor. I'm thinking Frustration, Outrage, or Resentment. Any good ideas?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-10-2023, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T14:03:31-08:00","id":1526627,"title":"","content":"I've also mulling over the Chronicle Tenets. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> that Tribe bans are a bit of questionable design. They don't have any precedence in the setting and they're not particularly interesting, but require unnecessary book keeping. So, I'm thinking about removing them altogether, especially since I'd rather have pack patrons back. Now, a pack patron ban does have precedence and is easier to handle because it's applicable to the whole group.<br /> <br /> In effect, I'm thinking about removing Tribe bans, having two regular &quot;Garou should never...&quot; tenets and one pack patron ban.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, what do you think are appropriate benefits from a pack patron? Should I just import/adapt the old &quot;totems,&quot; including making Patron a background?<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Okay, thinking more about it, I'll remove Tribe Bans <b>and</b> Favors. Tribe Bans will become a ban from the pack patron (in the form of a Chronicle Tenet). Tribe Favors will be replaced by the additional successes on Brutal outcomes for Auspice and Tribe verbs. However, how Tribe Favors work in RAW will serve as a template for benefits from pack patrons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-10-2023, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T16:16:21-08:00","id":1526638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526627#post1526627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In effect, I'm thinking about removing Tribe bans, having two regular &quot;Garou should never...&quot; tenets and one pack patron ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Another benefit of this system is that it's easy to modulate. This moves the Tenets away from an indication of a general tone, mood and atmosphere and more towards a reflection on the actual setting. Like here, it's more about setting up Tenets about Garou. With V5, for example, having a Tenet like &quot;Thou shalt not kill.&quot; in a struggle between Humanity and the Beast it might seem quite obvious what sort of conflict is set up. But with a more arcane concept like Garou the process is more guided as to help bring out the actual themes of the game. So it can't just be this freewheelin' thing anymore.<br /> <br /> But this model also has room to be expanded for fans of old lore. There's no limit to the number of Tenets and what sort of questions are linked to them. They need to work for the people you're playing with - but they also need to work for the game you're playing. Chronicle Tenets is a concept that can be guided by by a game's thematic boundaries and themes but ultimately it's molded by the people at the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Also, what do you think are appropriate benefits from a pack patron? Should I just import/adapt the old &quot;totems,&quot; including making Patron a background? </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest there are two ideas that I have in that regard: First, translate Coterie-Types to W5 as Pack-Types with a focus on Pack-Patron-Spirits. Second, translate expanded Coterie-creation-rules/Domain-management-rules to the Caern-management-system. Third, make it all more Blades In The Dark Crew-sheets-like. Justin Achilli mentioned that this was his inspiration for abandoning Pack-Types and introducing the caern-management-system instead, anyway. Who knows what happened behind the scenes but the actual system in the W5 corebook for caerns sucks.<br /> <br /> But that's... quite a bit of work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT 2: Okay, thinking more about it, I'll remove Tribe Bans <b>and</b> Favors. Tribe Bans will become a ban from the pack patron (in the form of a Chronicle Tenet). Tribe Favors will be replaced by the additional successes on Brutal outcomes for Auspice and Tribe verbs. However, how Tribe Favors work in RAW will serve as a template for benefits from pack patrons. </div> </div> </div>You don't need to do that, I think. Tribe-Favors is another inconsistent writing-project in the book but the solution is simple, I think. There's already a system in the game that gives you a situational bonus-die: Skill-Specializations. So that's what you turn it into instead: Every PC can pick from three Skills associated with a Tribe and get one free Skill-Specializiation. If it's a skill with no dots, you get a free dot and the Specialization.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you look at the wording of these Tribe-Favors, that's what they were essentially aiming for anyway. Personally, I'm a fan of a bonus-die only tied to a situation without being linked to a Skill as a Tribe-Favor but trying to figure that out for all 11 Tribes is a lot of work. Also, the irony is that giving a free Skill-Specialization offers more freedom for interpretation as well. If you want to deemphasize lore/worldbuilding the free Skill-Specialization makes way more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T18:02:16-08:00","id":1526644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526627#post1526627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT 2: Okay, thinking more about it, I'll remove Tribe Bans <b>and</b> Favors. Tribe Bans will become a ban from the pack patron (in the form of a Chronicle Tenet). Tribe Favors will be replaced by the additional successes on Brutal outcomes for Auspice and Tribe verbs. However, how Tribe Favors work in RAW will serve as a template for benefits from pack patrons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Merging Bans with the Tenets is an interesting idea. Could maybe some kind of a subvariant of tenets be used to explore the space of how Auspices work and are supposed to express their purpose? Maybe the Auspices having Tenets of their own that would affect Renown?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T01:12:41-08:00","id":1526657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526638#post1526638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to do that, I think. Tribe-Favors is another inconsistent writing-project in the book but the solution is simple, I think. There's already a system in the game that gives you a situational bonus-die: Skill-Specializations. So that's what you turn it into instead: Every PC can pick from three Skills associated with a Tribe and get one free Skill-Specializiation. If it's a skill with no dots, you get a free dot and the Specialization.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you look at the wording of these Tribe-Favors, that's what they were essentially aiming for anyway. Personally, I'm a fan of a bonus-die only tied to a situation without being linked to a Skill as a Tribe-Favor but trying to figure that out for all 11 Tribes is a lot of work. Also, the irony is that giving a free Skill-Specialization offers more freedom for interpretation as well. If you want to deemphasize lore/worldbuilding the free Skill-Specialization makes way more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to figure out the right skills for each tribe. This is what I have. Any suggestions for improvement? <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTableGrid\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Tribe</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Skills</span></b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Black Furies</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Brawl, Larceny, Leadership\u200b</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Bone Gnawers</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Awareness, Investigation, Streetwise</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Children of Gaia</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Awareness, Insight, Medicine</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Galestalkers</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Athletics, Stealth, Survival</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Ghost Council</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Investigation, Occult, Subterfuge</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Glass Walkers</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Finance, Technology, Science</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Hart Wardens</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Animal Ken, Craft, Survival</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Red Talons</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Awareness, Brawl, Survival</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Shadow Lords</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Intimidation, Subterfuge, Politics</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Silent Striders</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Athletics, Larceny, Stealth </span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b>Silver Fangs</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Leadership, Persuasion, Politics</span></td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b<br /> <br /> EDIT: And here's the first version of the Auspice adverbs. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTableGrid\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Auspice</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Original Verbs</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Revised Adverbs</span></b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Ragabash</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Trick, Misdirect, Mock, Sneak</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Cleverly, Provocatively, Subtly</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Theurge</span></span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Summon, Invoke, Placate, Bind</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Intuitively, Meticulously, Ritualistically</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Philodox</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Evaluate, Interpret, Punish, Judge</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Deliberately, Diplomatically, Even-handedly</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Galliard</span></span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Regale, Hype, Unite, Bluster</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Eloquently, Flamboyantly, Upliftingly</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Ahroun</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Fight, Attack, Destroy, Charge</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Bluntly, Courageously, Relentlessly</span></td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: With regard to the tribe verbs, I didn't feel particularly creative. I just deleted one of the more redundant verbs in the list. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTableGrid\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Tribe</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Verbs</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #f4b083\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">Revised Verbs</span></b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Black Furies</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Avenge, Overcome, Dismantle, Demolish</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Avenge, Dismantle, Demolish</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Bone Gnawers</span></span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">