MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Journey, Scout, Deliver, Sabotage</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\" style=\"background-color: #fbe4d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"color:black\">Scout, Deliver, Sabotage</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Silver Fangs</span></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Motivate, Lead, Rally, Inspire</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Motivate, Lead, Rally</span></td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-11-2023, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T01:15:05-08:00","id":1526658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526644#post1526644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Merging Bans with the Tenets is an interesting idea. Could maybe some kind of a subvariant of tenets be used to explore the space of how Auspices work and are supposed to express their purpose? Maybe the Auspices having Tenets of their own that would affect Renown?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's something <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> suggested above. My problem is that it would create the situation that Chronicle Tenets change depending on the individual (based on their Auspice in this case). Personally, I prefer Chronicle Tenets to be applicable to the whole group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T08:05:36-08:00","id":1526677,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/1tt3tyx1t3ektvci2uk1i/House-Rules-1.4.pdf?rlkey=w8ijl5e3cxxpsp0is396xub94&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Updated version of the house rules. </a>(Dropbox link)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Cleaned up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-12-2023, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T02:54:07-08:00","id":1526695,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Skills... Having thought about it, the only one I would change is the Black Furies one to &quot;Brawl, Athletics, Persuasion&quot;. One of the verbs is &quot;demolish&quot;, so Brawl, then &quot;overcome&quot; in the physical sense is represented by Athletics and then the whole angle of opposing someone in a position of power is better represented by Persuasion, I think, rather than Leadership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T13:20:36-08:00","id":1526713,"title":"","content":"I think in general the Auspice Adverbs look good, I feel like the Theurge and Philodox ones are a bit lacking. I would drop Meticulously (which overlaps a lot with Ritualistically anyway) for something like Contemplatively. Theurges are expected to be mystics and healers, and even if many focus on more empathetic/intuitive styles, stopping to meditate on a problem feels like it should be worked in somehow.<br /> <br /> The Philodox list feels very repetitive. There's nothing representing the investigatory, or punishment sides of the Auspice: all three adverbs are just variations on being thoughtful mediators. I would keep Deliberately (not every Philodox is tactful or fair). I would add something like Academically or Logically (how they debate about Garou morals, traditions, etc. and it's a nice contrast to the Theurges in regards to them having Intuitively), and something like Firmly (they want to stand by their judgements, ensure punishments are meted out, and make sure rules are followed, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T14:03:57-08:00","id":1526716,"title":"","content":"Great suggestions from both of you, thanks! I changed them accordingly.<br /> <br /> What do you think about the sum of the house rules? Do you think they fix some of W5's problems for you? Would you play in a chronicle using them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T06:24:40-08:00","id":1526740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526716#post1526716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great suggestions from both of you, thanks! I changed them accordingly.<br /> <br /> What do you think about the sum of the house rules? Do you think they fix some of W5's problems for you? Would you play in a chronicle using them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only other thing that I think needs to be addressed is the caern-management-system. It only becomes an issue in a longer campaign, I imagine, but I don't think the system quite makes sense.<br /> <br /> So the caerns have a rating of 1 to 5 and are defined like this on pg 192: &quot;The Caern Value Trait represents the power of that connection. A caern with Caern Value 1 may be a small, local, or specialized caern, whereas a caern with Caern Value 5 is one of the most powerful, spiritually resonant places on Earth.\u200b&quot; That definition seems strange, though, because the way the Rite of Caern Building works is you do the Rite, pay the XP cost (which is &quot;New Caern Level x 5&quot;) and raise the Caern Value and then you can pick one (!) new caern trait. But in that system a Value 5 caern (which according to the description would make it one of the most powerful caerns in the world) would at maximum have 5 caern traits and if you look at the list of traits most of them end the description with &quot;This Trait can be taken multiple times.&quot;. That seems contradictory. Why would you make caern-traits this limited in choice but then present so many traits that are supposed to be taken multiple times?<br /> <br /> There are multiple ways to resolve this but it needs to be considered in some way. Because I can't imagine any group getting to the point of investing narratively in going for a caern, then spend the XP for the two important Rites and the XP for raising the caern value to 1 - and then immediately being confronted by these limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T12:29:54-08:00","id":1526771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526740#post1526740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the caerns have a rating of 1 to 5 and are defined like this on pg 192: &quot;The Caern Value Trait represents the power of that connection. A caern with Caern Value 1 may be a small, local, or specialized caern, whereas a caern with Caern Value 5 is one of the most powerful, spiritually resonant places on Earth.\u200b&quot; That definition seems strange, though, because the way the Rite of Caern Building works is you do the Rite, pay the XP cost (which is &quot;New Caern Level x 5&quot;) and raise the Caern Value and then you can pick one (!) new caern trait. But in that system a Value 5 caern (which according to the description would make it one of the most powerful caerns in the world) would at maximum have 5 caern traits and if you look at the list of traits most of them end the description with &quot;This Trait can be taken multiple times.&quot;. That seems contradictory. Why would you make caern-traits this limited in choice but then present so many traits that are supposed to be taken multiple times?<br /> <br /> There are multiple ways to resolve this but it needs to be considered in some way. Because I can't imagine any group getting to the point of investing narratively in going for a caern, then spend the XP for the two important Rites and the XP for raising the caern value to 1 - and then immediately being confronted by these limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't want to tackle this quite yet, but mostly because I don't know how much I like it in the first place to give this much player control over a caern.<br /> <br /> In my old adventures/chronicles, caerns were very important for the story but--as central fixtures of the chronicle and its themes/mood--they were always firmly under the ST's control. In the end, changing a caern was part of the story, not something you simply solved mechanically.<br /> <br /> In my current V5 chronicle, I have a very ambivalent view about some backgrounds/advantages (e.g., Haven or Allies) having been made much more expensive... or rather less effective in comparison to older editions. I still allow players to buy backgrounds/advantages, mostly concerning their individual characters, but also freely grant them (e.g., Mawla) based on what happens in the story.<br /> <br /> So, on the one hand, the caern system seems kinda pointless for me. On the other hand, maybe there are situations where it makes sense to engage with the caern system. I'll have to see it in play and think about it though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T17:16:28-08:00","id":1526822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526771#post1526771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I didn't want to tackle this quite yet, but mostly because I don't know how much I like it in the first place to give this much player control over a caern.<br /> <br /> In my old adventures/chronicles, caerns were very important for the story but--as central fixtures of the chronicle and its themes/mood--they were always firmly under the ST's control. In the end, changing a caern was part of the story, not something you simply solved mechanically.<br /> <br /> In my current V5 chronicle, I have a very ambivalent view about some backgrounds/advantages (e.g., Haven or Allies) having been made much more expensive... or rather less effective in comparison to older editions. I still allow players to buy backgrounds/advantages, mostly concerning their individual characters, but also freely grant them (e.g., Mawla) based on what happens in the story.<br /> <br /> So, on the one hand, the caern system seems kinda pointless for me. On the other hand, maybe there are situations where it makes sense to engage with the caern system. I'll have to see it in play and think about it though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would've preferred Pack-Types as an analog to Coterie-Types rather than the move to this caern-system. And I think WOD5E should go way further in making group-types a thing, like for Coteries or Packs. You're not just picking neat little bonuses for your char-sheet, this is about the group of players at the table picking what aspect of the setting they're interested in. These should be packages of skills, powers and abilities (of course the terminology and structure) changes with the splat) that enable player-character-concepts to fit into whatever the group-concept is. I always thought that the Coterie-Types of Fugitive and Nomads were interesting because with those it isn't about bonuses and abilities but about a mode of play. No group will pick the Fugitive Coterie-Type because it's good for &quot;powergaming&quot; or something. Instead the Fugitive Coterie-Type is a package for characters playing out that type of story.<br /> <br /> Pack-Types could've been something similar. And then like in the V5 Players Guide you could've had an expanded system about caern-management like the expanded Coterie-system in the V5 Players Guide which is about Domain-management.<br /> <br /> But neither H5 nor W5 reproduced Coterie-Types for their splats, so who knows how that will look with the next splat... Certainly doesn't seem like Coterie-Types have a lot of fans over there at Paradox these days.<br /> <br /> And then there's of course the irony that all this lore/worldbuilding from past editions was erased to &quot;open up&quot; the game but then you get this new version which immediately gets bound and limited by directives like &quot;street-level-only&quot; and the game's insistence PC-groups better get invested in managing a caern...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T07:45:50-08:00","id":1526849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk?p=1526822#post1526822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would've preferred Pack-Types as an analog to Coterie-Types rather than the move to this caern-system. And I think WOD5E should go way further in making group-types a thing, like for Coteries or Packs. You're not just picking neat little bonuses for your char-sheet, this is about the group of players at the table picking what aspect of the setting they're interested in. These should be packages of skills, powers and abilities (of course the terminology and structure) changes with the splat) that enable player-character-concepts to fit into whatever the group-concept is. I always thought that the Coterie-Types of Fugitive and Nomads were interesting because with those it isn't about bonuses and abilities but about a mode of play. No group will pick the Fugitive Coterie-Type because it's good for &quot;powergaming&quot; or something. Instead the Fugitive Coterie-Type is a package for characters playing out that type of story.<br /> <br /> Pack-Types could've been something similar. And then like in the V5 Players Guide you could've had an expanded system about caern-management like the expanded Coterie-system in the V5 Players Guide which is about Domain-management.<br /> <br /> But neither H5 nor W5 reproduced Coterie-Types for their splats, so who knows how that will look with the next splat... Certainly doesn't seem like Coterie-Types have a lot of fans over there at Paradox these days.<br /> <br /> And then there's of course the irony that all this lore/worldbuilding from past editions was erased to &quot;open up&quot; the game but then you get this new version which immediately gets bound and limited by directives like &quot;street-level-only&quot; and the game's insistence PC-groups better get invested in managing a caern...</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, the more I think about it, the more I like your idea. We haven't used the Coterie system in V5 yet, because the PCs just managed to establish themselves (next part of the chronicle, they will have their own domain), so I gotta read up on it anyway. I will read up on the caern system again as well, and compare it to Revised/W20.<br /> <br /> The only thing that went through my mind when I looked through the coterie types in the V5 Players Guide was what type of packs there are in WtA in the first place... I mean, I have some ideas (monkey wrenchers, attack pack, caern guardians, etc.) but I would appreciate you sharing your ideas about which types you think should exist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}